```js
const tickets = [
  { id: 'T-1', status: 'open' },
  { id: 'T-2', status: 'closed' },
];

// filter builds a NEW array; `tickets` is unchanged afterwards.
const open = tickets.filter((ticket) => ticket.status === 'open');

open.length;    // 1
tickets.length; // still 2
```

The predicate answers one question per record: keep it, or not. Because `filter` returns a new array, you can chain a second selection without disturbing the first result.
